# PowerShell Modules

## Layout

- One function per file: `lib/<Module>/<Verb>-Inspera<Noun>.ps1`
- Loader: `lib/<Module>.ps1` dot-sources all `lib/<Module>/*.ps1` sorted by name
- `lib/Common/00-State.ps1` loads first (script-scope state)
- Entry scripts stay thin: dot-source loader → call one `Invoke-Inspera*Toolkit` → exit with result code

## Dependency order

`Common` → `LogParser` → `ProcessManager` → `SystemChecks` → `ToolkitActions` / `ToolkitGui`

Loaders pull prerequisites automatically. Dot-source pattern:

```powershell
. (Join-Path $libDir 'Common.ps1')
```

## Common change paths

| Change | Touch |
|---|---|
| New log line format | `Parse-InsperaLogLine.ps1` → `Parse-InsperaLog.ps1` / `Select-InsperaPrimaryFailure.ps1` |
| New system check | `lib/SystemChecks/Test-Inspera*.ps1` + wire in `Invoke-InsperaSystemChecks.ps1` or `Invoke-InsperaTargetedChecks.ps1` |
| New toolkit flow | `lib/ToolkitActions/Invoke-Inspera*.ps1` |
| GUI change | `lib/ToolkitGui/` + rebuild exe |

## Paths

Use `Get-InsperaRoot`, `Get-InsperaAppRoot`, `Get-InsperaLibPath`, `Get-InsperaDataPath` — not hardcoded repo paths (exe-aware at runtime).
